        b


    {\displaystyle b}

, then the Lamport timestamp of 



        a


    {\displaystyle a}

 will be less than the Lamport timestamp of 



        b


    {\displaystyle b}

. It’s also possible to have two events where we can’t say which came first; when that happens, it means that they couldn’t have affected each other. If 



        a


    {\displaystyle a}

 and 



